title: 'relay auth: intermittent Ed25519 request signature does not verify after rename/register'
updated_at: "2026-07-14T08:41:37Z"
---
## Problem
During post-rename relay recovery, c2c whoami --relay sometimes reports: Ed25519 request signature does not verify, then later succeeds after re-register. Unclear if race with lease propagation, key/path confusion after alias change, or clock/nonce interaction (see also B178 timestamp skew).

## Expected
Signature verification failures should be rare, explained (which key, which payload field), and self-recovering or with a single clear remediation.

## Actual
Transient auth failure mixed with identity-binding and connector-down states makes multi-step recovery guesswork.

## Related
B178 (timestamp_out_of_window / nonce_replay), rename re-register gap, connector bridge liveness.

## Suggested fix
Log verify failure reason code; ensure rename/register uses one identity key consistently; retry-once on propagation delay with jitter; never leave whoami in opaque verify-fail without next step.